        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: keep bounded Unicode text valid across UTF-16 boundaries",
        "body": "Supersedes #102669, #102671, #102672, #102674, #102685, #102695, #102696, #102697, #102715, #102719, #102720, #102721, #102722, #102723, #102734, #102737, and #102741.\n\nAlso preserves the useful unique changes from closed #102667, #102767, #102774, and #102775.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where bounded text could end or begin with half of a UTF-16 surrogate pair when an emoji or supplementary-plane character crossed a size limit. Depending on the consumer, that could surface as a replacement character in user-visible errors, labels, diagnostics, stored artifacts, model prompts, QA evidence, or Control UI previews.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis consolidates the remaining real call sites onto the existing UTF-16-safe slicing primitives while preserving each surface's established UTF-16-unit budget and `undefined` versus empty-string semantics. It also makes head-plus-tail previews safe at both boundaries, keeps the QA Lab browser build source-resolvable, and carries the exact compacted-prefix boundary through tool-call stream suppression so safe slicing cannot weaken terminal snapshot scrubbing.\n\n## User Impact\n\nEmoji and supplementary-plane text now remains valid when these bounded previews, labels, filenames, errors, and prompts are truncated. No configuration or migration is required.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Standalone clean-source QA Lab Vite build passed on Blacksmith Testbox.\n- Focused Testbox run passed 6 Vitest shards, including 125 unit-fast assertions plus hooks, auto-reply, UI, WhatsApp, and QA Lab suites: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29019077492\n- Exact follow-up stream/label regression run passed 67 tool-call stream tests and 9 conversation-label tests: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29019254011\n- Exact follow-up media/QA run passed 48 media-store tests and 9 QA Lab UI tests: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29019373020\n- Full production build, including plugin SDK exports and Control UI, passed on Blacksmith Testbox: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29019579334\n- Dependency report: only two intentional workspace links plus their importer lockfile entries; 0 added, removed, or version-changed resolved packages.\n- Exact-head hosted CI: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29020160706 (pending; native prepare will require success before merge).\n- Fresh autoreview: no accepted/actionable findings after repairing the compacted-buffer state and QA Lab build-resolution findings.\n- Independent source review: no remaining findings across the consolidated diff.\n",
